      "t": "Oui?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes?' Sofia answers the door with a brief question.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gabriel",
      "t": "Sofia? Excuse-moi, je te dérange?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Sofia? Sorry, am I disturbing you?' Gabriel apologizes at Sofia's door and asks if he is disturbing her.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "sofia",
      "t": "Non, tu ne me déranges pas.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, you aren't bothering me.' Sofia assures him that he is not bothering her at all.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gabriel",
      "t": "Je devais te voir.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I had to see you.' Gabriel explains that he could not go home without seeing her first.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gabriel",
      "t": "Je me sens vraiment mal pour tout à l'heure.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I feel really bad about earlier.' Gabriel admits how terrible he feels about their argument earlier that day.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "sofia",
      "t": "Ce que j'ai dit était horrible.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What I said was horrible.' Sofia apologizes for losing her temper during their earlier fight.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gabriel",
      "t": "Non, j'aurais dû te le dire.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'No, I should have told you.' Gabriel insists the fault was his for not warning her about the choreography.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "sofia",
      "t": "Tu veux boire quelque chose?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Do you want to drink something?' Sofia invites Gabriel inside for a drink to make peace.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gabriel",
      "t": "Oui, volontiers.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, gladly.' Gabriel happily accepts her invitation to come in.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "sofia",
      "t": "J'ai du porto.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I have some port.' Sofia offers him a glass of port wine.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gabriel",
      "t": "J'adore le porto.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I love port.' French verbs of preference take a definite article.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "andrea",
      "t": "Gabriel!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Gabriel! Open up!' Andrea pounds frantically on Gabriel's apartment door late at night.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gabriel",
      "t": "Andréa? Tu es blessée?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Andréa? Are you hurt?' Gabriel opens his door to find Andréa soaking wet and asks if she is hurt.",
      "gap": 0.4
